# Database & Migrations

- Source of truth for structure while coding: **`database/schema.sql`**
- Schema changes: create `database/migrations/YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_description.sql` (TiDB Cloud Serverless / MySQL 8.0 compatible)
- After apply: update `database/schema.sql` to match
- Credentials: `.env` (`DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_USER`, `DB_PASSWORD`, `DB_NAME`)
- Always connect with `--ssl-mode=REQUIRED --protocol=TCP`
- `DB_SSL=true` is required for TiDB Cloud

```bash
npm run db:migrate
```

```bash
DB_PASS=$(grep "^DB_PASSWORD" .env | cut -d'=' -f2-) && \
DB_HOST=$(grep "^DB_HOST" .env | cut -d'=' -f2-) && \
DB_PORT=$(grep "^DB_PORT" .env | cut -d'=' -f2-) && \
DB_USER=$(grep "^DB_USER" .env | cut -d'=' -f2-) && \
DB_NAME=$(grep "^DB_NAME" .env | cut -d'=' -f2-) && \
mysql -h "$DB_HOST" -P "$DB_PORT" -u "$DB_USER" -p"$DB_PASS" "$DB_NAME" \
  --ssl-mode=REQUIRED --protocol=TCP \
  < database/migrations/YOUR_MIGRATION_FILE.sql
```

- Map DB errors to friendly API responses (409 duplicate, 400 FK) — never leak raw MySQL/TiDB messages like `Duplicate entry '?'`
- TiDB Serverless drops idle sockets — do not hold connections across long deploys
- phpMyAdmin dumps that `ALTER TABLE … MODIFY id AUTO_INCREMENT` fail on TiDB (error 8200). Bootstrap with `scripts/apply-schema-tidb.sh` (rewrites CREATE TABLE first)
- Incremental changes go in `database/migrations/` and `npm run db:migrate`
